From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jffs2: use <linux/stddef.h> for in-kernel LZMA SDK builds

Select kernel stddef header under __KERNEL__ to prevent host stddef collisions.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/lzma/Types.h
+++ b/include/linux/lzma/Types.h
@@ -4,7 +4,11 @@
 #ifndef __7Z_TYPES_H
 #define __7Z_TYPES_H
 
+#ifdef __KERNEL__
+#include <linux/stddef.h>
+#else
 #include <stddef.h>
+#endif
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <windows.h>
